  "goodToKnow": "Der Feldherr is a historical military commander or general, used for figures like Hannibal, Caesar or Frederick the Great. Like Herr, it takes -n in the singular oblique cases (den, dem, des Feldherrn) and -en in the plural. Munich's Feldherrnhalle honours Bavarian generals; Hitler's failed 1923 putsch ended there. Das Feldherrntalent means talent for leadership. Plural: die Feldherren."
